From: Johannes <johannes.hirche@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:34:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Add -OutputSRGB to write sRGB DDS formats

There was no way to get sRGB DXGI formats out of the CLI: CMP_FORMAT has
no sRGB BC variants and the DDS writer only produced *_UNORM formats, so
sRGB textures lost their color space (BC7 was written as BC7_UNORM, BC1-3
with legacy FourCC headers that can't express sRGB at all).

-OutputSRGB (CMP_CompressOptions::outputSRGB) marks the output mip set
with the new MS_FLAG_sRGB. The DDS writer then uses a DX10 header with
BC1/BC2/BC3/BC7_UNORM_SRGB or R8G8B8A8_UNORM_SRGB. Formats without an
sRGB variant are written as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
